   "kind": "concept",
   "headingEn": "The direct object goes in the accusative",
   "en": "In a sentence like \"She reads a newspaper,\" the newspaper is the thing being read — the direct object. Russian puts the direct object into a special form called the accusative case. Often the word changes its ending to signal \"this is the target of the action.\"",
   "noteEn": "English marks the object by word order (I see him, not I see he). Russian marks it by ending."
