   "kind": "concept",
   "headingEn": "Nouns come in genders",
   "en": "Every Russian noun has a gender: masculine, feminine, or neuter. дом (house) is masculine, машина (car) is feminine, окно (window) is neuter. The adjective looks at that gender and picks the matching tail. This matching is called agreement."
