   "headingEn": "Why goodbyes talk about meeting again",
   "en": "English 'goodbye' hides a blessing ('God be with ye'). Russian до свидания is sunnier: it points to the next meeting, not the parting. Many Russian farewells work this way — they promise reunion rather than mourn the exit.",
   "noteEn": "Knowing the meaning ('until the meeting') helps the spelling stick — свидания shares a root with 'видеть', to see."
