   "en": "In English 'please' and 'you're welcome' are separate. Russian lets 'пожалуйста' cover both — it's the all-purpose politeness word. So if someone says 'спасибо' and you hear 'paZHALsta' bounce back, it's 'you're welcome'; if it comes before a request, it's 'please'. Context decides.",
