   "en": "Put the beat in the wrong place and a Russian ear may not recognize your word at all — even if every letter is right. Stress also reshapes the vowels around it: unstressed vowels get shorter and blurrier. So the beat isn't decoration; it's the skeleton the whole word hangs on."
