   "headingEn": "The six people a verb can point to",
   "en": "Every conjugated verb points at one of six 'slots': the speaker (I / we), the listener (you — one or many), or someone else (he, she / they). Russian has a pronoun for each slot, and these six little words unlock every conjugation table you will ever meet. Here they are, arranged the way Russians think of them."
