   "headingEn": "Why «вы» is capitalized sometimes",
   "en": "In letters and polite writing you'll see «Вы» with a capital V even mid-sentence. It's a mark of respect, like tipping your hat to the reader. Speaking, you can't hear the capital — but knowing it's there explains why the same little word carries such weight.",
   "noteEn": "Same sound \"vy\" whether it's polite-single or plural."
