   "en": "Normal Russian adjectives agree with their noun in gender, number and case — that is a lot of endings. But a comparative like интереснее is not describing a noun directly; it sits after 'to be' or beside a verb, doing a job closer to an adverb. Words in that slot don't agree, so they never inflect."
