   "headingEn": "Why absence needs the genitive",
   "en": "\"There is no book\" is нет книги, not нет книга. English marks absence with a word (\"no\"); Russian marks it on the noun itself, in the genitive. Logic: to say a thing is missing, you name it \"of\" the empty set — so it goes genitive. нет always pulls its noun into the genitive.",
