   "headingEn": "Why -ом becomes -ем after soft stems",
   "en": "Russian dislikes a hard 'o' sitting right after a soft consonant — the two fight in the mouth. So after anything soft (ь, й, or a soft consonant) the о relaxes into е. Same word-ending, just a softer vowel to match a softer stem.",
   "noteEn": "учитель ends in a soft ь, so учителем, never учителом."
