   "kind": "why",
   "headingEn": "Why stress flips the vowel back",
   "en": "When the ending is unstressed after a husher/ц, Russian defaults to the softer-looking е. But when the stress lands ON the ending, the full, strong о survives — you can actually hear it: нож-ОМ. So the rule is really 'quiet ending → е, loud ending → о'.",
   "noteEn": "Say ножом out loud — the -ом is stressed and clear."
