   "headingEn": "Why a prefix means 'finished'",
   "en": "A prefix originally added a direction or endpoint — на- suggests putting something onto a surface, писать 'to write' plus на- gives 'to write it onto (the page), get it down'. An action aimed at an endpoint naturally implies reaching that endpoint. Over centuries that 'reaching the endpoint' hardened into pure completion meaning.",
