   "headingEn": "Why examiners reward it",
   "en": "An unhedged 'Это доказывает, что…' ('This proves that…') sounds naïve to a Russian examiner — real data rarely proves anything outright. Hedging shows you understand the limits of your evidence, which reads as intellectual maturity, not weakness."
