   "headingEn": "What the snow idiom conveys",
   "en": "как снег на голову describes an event that is sudden and totally unexpected — and usually unwelcome. It's the shock, not just the surprise.",
   "ru": "Новость свалилась как снег на голову.",
   "translit": "Nóvost' svalílas' kak sneg na gólovu.",
   "noteEn": "Often paired with свалиться / упасть ('to fall on'), reinforcing the image of something dropping on you."
