   "kind": "why",
   "headingEn": "Why 'commit a mistake' feels elevated",
   "en": "совершить carries a note of finality — it's used for accomplished acts (совершить подвиг = perform a feat, совершить ошибку = commit an error). That weight is exactly why it suits formal writing, where a flat делать ошибку sounds too casual.",
   "noteEn": "Register matters: совершить/допустить for formal, делать only in loose speech."
