   "headingEn": "Why learn phrase-pairs, not single lines",
   "en": "Many formulas exist only as answers to other formulas. Ни пуха ни пера! is incomplete without К чёрту!; Спасибо invites Не за что. Storing them as pairs means the right reply is automatic, so you never freeze or improvise something non-native.",
   "noteEn": "Elaborate on the pair, not the isolated word — that's how fluent speakers store them."
