   "headingEn": "The neutral default: S–V–O",
   "en": "With no special context, a plain declarative runs Subject–Verb–Object, and the rheme lands naturally at the end. «Студент пишет диктант» — student (theme) → writes → dictation (the new bit). Start from S–V–O, then bend it on purpose.",
   "noteEn": "S–V–O is your home base, not a straitjacket."
