   "kind": "tip",
   "headingEn": "In short",
   "en": "Case does the grammar, so order is free to manage information · Neutral flow = theme first (known), rheme last (new) · To emphasize, push a word to the END, never front it English-style · Use the 'what question does it answer?' test — the answering word goes last.",
   "noteEn": "Master the end slot and you control the whole message."
