   "kind": "why",
   "headingEn": "Why bureaucrats love nouns",
   "en": "A verb needs a doer: «Иванов нарушил» names a culprit. A noun hides one: «зафиксировано нарушение» reports a violation with no accuser attached. Nominalization lets a document state facts without pointing fingers — which is exactly what laws, findings, and notices are designed to do.",
