   "kind": "why",
   "headingEn": "Why the intriguing opening works",
   "en": "«Казалось бы…» means 'one would think…' — and it always sets up a 'but'. It's a rhetorical trapdoor: you state the obvious answer only to pull it away. Examiners reward it because it shows you can hold two viewpoints at once, the core of рассуждение (reasoning).",
   "ru": "Казалось бы, ответ очевиден, однако всё гораздо сложнее.",
   "noteEn": "«Казалось» here is the past form of the intrigue formula «Казалось бы» — the tested opener."
