   "headingEn": "Inversion: word order as a tool",
   "en": "Russian's free word order turns инверсия — leaving the neutral order — into an expressive lever. Put the adjective AFTER its noun, «ночь тёмная», «тоска зелёная», and you summon a folk-poetic, solemn colouring. The neutral «тёмная ночь» would sound flat by comparison.",
   "noteEn": "Neutral order informs; marked order colours and emphasises."
