   "en": "Quote a line with the same charge its source gave it. An ironic line stays ironic; a lofty line stays lofty. Quoting an ironic line as if it were sincere is the single clearest way to mark yourself as non-native — the words are right, but the intent is wrong.",
   "noteEn": "Register and connotation travel with the phrase. This is the fact the whole lesson protects."
