   "en": "'He gave to the cause his life, his talent, his health — and two thousand roubles in fines.' The solemn tricolon (life, talent, health) sets up a heroic sacrifice; the dash then drops us onto a parking-ticket fine. That abrupt descent from the exalted to the trivial is бато́с.",
   "noteEn": "The dash is the trapdoor — everything before it is bait."
