   "headingEn": "Why one word means TWO things",
   "ru": "Пожалуйста",
   "translit": "Pozhaluysta",
   "en": "Here's the twist: «пожалуйста» also means 'please.' At its root it means 'be so kind' — and being kind fits both directions. When YOU ask, it softens the request ('please'); when you REPLY, it grants the kindness ('you're welcome'). One idea, two uses."
